  },
  "notes": "The Qualla photographs establish the pale limestone east gable with buttresses, double-pitch slate roof and copper flèche, and the two stories and rows of red window frames of Munkklostret. The parish architectural survey identifies the west choir, sacristy, window form and portals. The state owner describes the materials and conservation of the nuns’ wings."
